      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GREAT TIMES AHEAD (3) goes on top in an open race after a Hawkesbury debut that had more merit than his price suggested. Unwanted in the market, he struck an early block but was good late. With that experience and blinkers first time, he has scope to improve sharply. WIN STAR (7) has put together placings at Doomben and Ipswich, the latest as a well-supported favourite. She has the right profile fourth-up if the 1500m does not stretch her. WURZBURG (4) needs to lift off an Ipswich fifth, but a close Deagon trial and natural improvement keep him in discussion. ANDER'S DREAM (5) has been safely held at Ipswich but is race fit, gets blinkers and can be more competitive if she runs out the trip.",
